<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zulfikar Ali Bhutto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1928">1928</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zulfikar Ali Bhutto was a Pakistani statesman who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> Peoples Party in 1967. After the loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-pakistan">East Pakistan</a> in 1971 he became president and then prime minister, nationalised industries, introduced the 1973 constitution and began Pakistan's nuclear programme. He was overthrown by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-zia-ul-haq">Zia-ul-Haq</a> in 1977 and hanged in 1979.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zulfikar-ali-bhutto.jpg" alt="Zulfikar Ali Bhutto" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer. Office of President Zulfikar Ali Bhutto. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Z_A_Bhutto_(President_of_Pakistan).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
